WEBVTT

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.422
What do you think of the view, Fry?

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:07.633
It really puts things in perspective.

00:00:07.758 --> 00:00:11.845
I mean, from up here, an entire world
can seem utterly insignificant.

00:00:50.475 --> 00:00:52.102
Hey, nice seats.

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:53.353
We're close enough that when you

00:00:53.437 --> 00:00:56.315
knock a player down with a beer bottle,
he stays down.

00:00:56.398 --> 00:00:57.399
I don't get this.

00:00:57.482 --> 00:00:59.902
Is Blernsball exactly
the same as baseball?

00:01:00.068 --> 00:01:02.279
Baseball? God forbid.

00:01:02.487 --> 00:01:06.491
Face it, Fry. Baseball was as boring
as mom and apple pie.

00:01:06.617 --> 00:01:07.826
That's why they jazzed it up.

00:01:07.951 --> 00:01:09.745
Boring? Baseball wasn't...

00:01:10.287 --> 00:01:12.247
Hmm, so they finally jazzed it up.

00:01:16.627 --> 00:01:17.669
Home run!

00:01:17.753 --> 00:01:19.087
Yay, yay!

00:01:19.171 --> 00:01:20.255
Right?

00:01:21.924 --> 00:01:22.966
Ugh.

00:01:24.718 --> 00:01:25.719
Out.

00:01:25.802 --> 00:01:28.013
Yeah! Yay!

00:01:28.513 --> 00:01:31.600
What just happened?
Why is the ball on that sproingy thing?

00:01:31.683 --> 00:01:35.562
It's traditional, just like aluminum bats
and the seventh-inning grope.

00:01:40.025 --> 00:01:41.818
Hey, hey, hey!

00:01:41.944 --> 00:01:43.779
I got me a souvenir.

00:01:45.489 --> 00:01:47.449
Aw, here you go, kid.

00:01:53.956 --> 00:01:56.375
I'd like a jumbo squid log, please.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:57.876
We don't sell those.

00:01:58.126 --> 00:01:59.169
All right, all right.

00:01:59.253 --> 00:02:01.421
Let me have one of your young on a roll.

00:02:01.713 --> 00:02:02.756
We're out of rolls.

00:02:03.006 --> 00:02:06.802
Fine. Just give me something
crawling with parasites.

00:02:09.888 --> 00:02:12.349
Hmm. At least hot dogs haven't changed.

00:02:12.808 --> 00:02:14.518
Hey, buddies, who wants popcorn?

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:16.645
- Oh, I'll have some.
- Oh, yeah. Popcorn.

00:02:20.899 --> 00:02:22.776
Anyone want butter on that?

00:02:24.861 --> 00:02:26.780
Hey, I'm starting to get
the hang of this game.

00:02:26.905 --> 00:02:28.240
The blerns are loaded,

00:02:28.323 --> 00:02:30.325
the count's three blerns
and two anti-blerns

00:02:30.409 --> 00:02:32.661
and the infield blern rule
is in effect. Right?

00:02:32.953 --> 00:02:35.664
Except for the word "blern,"
that was complete gibberish.

00:02:42.129 --> 00:02:43.130
Multi-ball!

00:02:43.463 --> 00:02:44.756
Multi-ball!

00:02:47.759 --> 00:02:49.011
Blern!

00:02:49.386 --> 00:02:53.599
Blern!

00:02:59.062 --> 00:03:01.481
All right! Yes!

00:03:01.732 --> 00:03:04.109
Miller's on a pace to hit 70 blerns.

00:03:04.192 --> 00:03:08.071
He's good all right,
but he's no Clem Johnson.

00:03:08.155 --> 00:03:09.865
And Johnson played back in the days

00:03:09.948 --> 00:03:12.743
before steroid injections were mandatory.

00:03:12.826 --> 00:03:14.119
Clem Johnson?

00:03:14.202 --> 00:03:16.830
That sack of skin
wouldn't have lasted one pitch

00:03:16.914 --> 00:03:18.457
in the old robot leagues.

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:20.667
Now, Wireless Joe Jackson...

00:03:20.834 --> 00:03:22.961
There was a blern-hitting machine.

00:03:23.045 --> 00:03:26.256
Exactly, he was a machine
designed to hit blerns.

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:28.717
I mean, come on, Wireless Joe was nothing

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:30.636
but a programmable bat on wheels.

00:03:30.802 --> 00:03:35.307
Oh, and I suppose pitch-o-mat 5000
was just a modified howitzer.

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:37.309
- Yep.
- You know, you humans are so scared

00:03:37.392 --> 00:03:40.896
of a little robot competition,
you won't even let us on the field.

00:03:40.979 --> 00:03:43.690
What are you talking about?
There's all kinds of robots down there.

00:03:43.857 --> 00:03:45.817
Yeah. Doing crap work.

00:03:45.901 --> 00:03:49.738
They're bat boys, ball polishers,
sprinkler systems,

00:03:49.905 --> 00:03:52.449
but how many robot managers are there?

00:03:52.658 --> 00:03:54.034
- Eleven?
- Zero!

00:03:55.494 --> 00:03:57.579
And what a surprise.

00:03:57.663 --> 00:03:59.665
Look who's scraping up the filth.

00:03:59.748 --> 00:04:01.375
Is it a human child?

00:04:01.458 --> 00:04:02.668
I wish.

00:04:03.126 --> 00:04:04.544
Whoa! Dear Lord!

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:09.091
- What's wrong?
- Oh, uh, it's... My... New pager.

00:04:11.468 --> 00:04:12.636
This is Hermes.

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:14.137
A package just came in.

00:04:14.221 --> 00:04:16.682
Everyone needs to return
to the office immediately.

00:04:20.394 --> 00:04:22.312
Get away, you filthy bird.

00:04:22.437 --> 00:04:24.856
Shoo! Shoo!Professor, turn me off quick.

00:04:25.065 --> 00:04:26.483
I'm sorry. What?

00:04:27.943 --> 00:04:29.528
See you at the office.

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:32.281
Admit it.

00:04:32.364 --> 00:04:34.157
You all think robots are just machines

00:04:34.241 --> 00:04:36.577
built by humans
to make their lives easier.

00:04:36.785 --> 00:04:37.828
Well, aren't they?

00:04:37.911 --> 00:04:41.123
I've never made anyone's life easier
and you know it.

00:04:41.623 --> 00:04:43.166
Great news, everyone.

00:04:43.292 --> 00:04:46.253
You'll be delivering
a package to Chapek 9.

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:48.964
A world where humans are killed on sight.

00:04:49.131 --> 00:04:50.632
Why is that great news?

00:04:50.924 --> 00:04:53.218
I'm glad you asked that question, Fry.

00:04:53.302 --> 00:04:56.847
You see, Chapek 9
was colonized centuries ago

00:04:56.930 --> 00:05:00.392
by a murderous crew
of radical robot separatists.

00:05:00.559 --> 00:05:03.228
Oh, so just 'cause a robot
wants to kill humans,

00:05:03.312 --> 00:05:05.063
that makes him a "radical."

00:05:05.272 --> 00:05:08.567
Hey, hold on.
I understand these robots hate humans,

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:10.777
but how do they feel
about humanoid aliens?

00:05:11.069 --> 00:05:12.404
They're not fans.

00:05:12.613 --> 00:05:15.157
That's why Bender
will have to make the actual delivery.

00:05:15.449 --> 00:05:19.161
Oh, I get it,
make the robot do all the work.

00:05:19.328 --> 00:05:22.706
This is the first actual work
you've ever had to do around here.

00:05:22.789 --> 00:05:24.249
Well, I'm not doing it.

00:05:24.374 --> 00:05:25.918
It's a robot holiday.

00:05:26.084 --> 00:05:27.252
Really? Which one?

00:05:27.502 --> 00:05:28.962
Only Robanukah...

00:05:29.046 --> 00:05:31.506
The holiest two weeks
on the robot calendar.

00:05:31.965 --> 00:05:33.884
Oh, come on, Bender.

00:05:33.967 --> 00:05:37.387
Last month it was Robamadan,
and before that Robanzaa.

00:05:37.471 --> 00:05:39.306
Man, that one was a blast.

00:05:39.431 --> 00:05:41.391
It wasn't just a blast.

00:05:41.558 --> 00:05:44.978
It was a sacred tribute
to my ancestral prototypes

00:05:45.062 --> 00:05:47.564
which happened to take the form
of a drinking contest.

00:05:47.814 --> 00:05:50.609
Now, look here, Bender,
I respect your diversity

00:05:50.692 --> 00:05:52.194
to the extent the law requires,

00:05:52.277 --> 00:05:56.114
but you used up all your days off
when you had that bout with roberculosis.

00:05:56.740 --> 00:05:59.368
Aw, all right, I'll go.

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:03.497
But so help me, I'll hold a grudge against
every last stinking one of you

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:05.207
for the rest of your lives.

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:06.500
Well, then it's settled.

00:06:06.583 --> 00:06:08.293
So long, everyone.

00:06:11.338 --> 00:06:14.633
So, let me get this straight.
This planet is completely uninhabited?

00:06:14.716 --> 00:06:17.844
No. It's inhabited by robots.

00:06:17.928 --> 00:06:21.223
Oh, kind of like how a warehouse
is inhabited by boxes.

00:06:23.767 --> 00:06:25.477
Okay, Bender, we're here.

00:06:25.561 --> 00:06:26.645
It's time to get to work.

00:06:26.728 --> 00:06:29.231
Yes, Miz Leela, tote that space barge,

00:06:29.314 --> 00:06:31.066
lift that space bale.

00:06:31.149 --> 00:06:32.818
Now, we can't land on the surface

00:06:32.901 --> 00:06:34.987
because those robots
would kill Fry and me.

00:06:35.153 --> 00:06:38.073
So, we'll have to stay up here
and lower you with the winch.

00:06:38.156 --> 00:06:40.576
And remember, you don't know humans,

00:06:40.659 --> 00:06:42.035
you don't work for humans,

00:06:42.119 --> 00:06:44.705
and above all, you don't like humans.

00:06:44.871 --> 00:06:47.374
I'll try to keep that in mind.

00:06:49.459 --> 00:06:51.545
Hmm, he seems pretty angry.

00:06:51.628 --> 00:06:53.755
Yeah, but I guess
I'd be kind of angry, too

00:06:53.839 --> 00:06:56.174
if I had to go to some uninhabited planet.

00:06:56.258 --> 00:06:58.135
Maybe we ought to do
something nice for him.

00:07:00.596 --> 00:07:04.141
There, this oughta show that stupid robot
we care about him.

00:07:05.434 --> 00:07:07.269
Ah, Bender must be done with the delivery.

00:07:08.770 --> 00:07:10.606
I... I'm in trouble.

00:07:10.689 --> 00:07:12.566
They found out I work with humans, and...

00:07:12.649 --> 00:07:14.109
Oh, no. Oh, no!

00:07:16.069 --> 00:07:18.238
Oh, my God.

00:07:18.322 --> 00:07:20.449
- We have to go down and rescue him.
- No, we can't.

00:07:20.532 --> 00:07:21.742
They'll kill us on sight.

00:07:21.825 --> 00:07:23.118
What are we going to do?

00:07:23.201 --> 00:07:26.413
I don't know. I don't know.
It's not an easy decision.

00:07:26.496 --> 00:07:29.458
If only I had two or three minutes
to think about it.

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:33.378
Okay. If we're going to save Bender

00:07:33.462 --> 00:07:35.964
we've got to look and act
exactly like robots.

00:07:36.048 --> 00:07:38.091
I am fully operational, Captain.

00:07:38.175 --> 00:07:40.761
We'll have to walk like robots,
talk like robots,

00:07:40.844 --> 00:07:44.556
and if necessary solve complex
differential equations like robots.

00:07:44.765 --> 00:07:47.184
I can sort of dance like a robot.
Will that help?

00:07:51.438 --> 00:07:54.524
Oh, Fry, first of all, this is serious.

00:07:54.650 --> 00:07:56.026
And second of all...

00:08:10.123 --> 00:08:11.959
Man, we look stupid.

00:08:12.042 --> 00:08:14.002
We should have gotten
store-bought costumes.

00:08:14.169 --> 00:08:16.964
Yeah, but there wasn't
a Woolworth's in this quadrant.

00:08:17.047 --> 00:08:18.131
Halt!

00:08:18.215 --> 00:08:20.759
Be you robot or human?

00:08:21.093 --> 00:08:22.803
Robot... We be.

00:08:22.970 --> 00:08:23.971
Uh, yep.

00:08:24.054 --> 00:08:26.557
Just two robots out roboting it up.

00:08:28.934 --> 00:08:30.018
Eh?

00:08:30.519 --> 00:08:32.729
Administer the test.

00:08:35.566 --> 00:08:37.818
Which of the following
would you most prefer:

00:08:37.901 --> 00:08:39.528
A, a puppy,

00:08:39.653 --> 00:08:42.114
B, a pretty flower from your sweetie,

00:08:42.197 --> 00:08:45.826
or C, a large
properly formatted data file?

00:08:45.909 --> 00:08:46.910
Choose!

00:08:49.997 --> 00:08:52.207
Uh, is the puppy mechanical in any way?

00:08:52.332 --> 00:08:55.252
No, it is the bad kind of puppy.

00:08:55.460 --> 00:08:57.045
Then we'll go with that data file.

00:08:57.337 --> 00:08:58.338
Correct.

00:08:58.422 --> 00:09:00.090
The flower would also
have been acceptable.

00:09:00.382 --> 00:09:01.592
You may pass.

00:09:08.348 --> 00:09:11.184
Now, if you see any robots
just stay out of their way.

00:09:25.949 --> 00:09:27.242
So far, so good.

00:09:29.328 --> 00:09:31.121
Little to the right... There you go.

00:09:31.788 --> 00:09:33.457
Have you seen this robot?

00:09:35.375 --> 00:09:36.793
Sorry, can't help you.

00:09:36.877 --> 00:09:38.086
Hey, watch it!

00:09:38.170 --> 00:09:39.922
Don't drop that there.

00:09:40.255 --> 00:09:41.757
Oh...

00:09:44.209 --> 00:09:46.670
Come on, Fry, walk like a robot.

00:09:46.795 --> 00:09:48.839
I can't. I have to go to the bathroom.

00:09:49.173 --> 00:09:50.841
Robots don't have bathrooms.

00:09:51.175 --> 00:09:52.217
Oh, right.

00:09:52.301 --> 00:09:54.261
I wonder where they smoke in high school?

00:09:54.386 --> 00:09:56.638
Listen, just go behind those garbage cans.

00:09:56.763 --> 00:09:57.764
I'll stand guard.

00:10:03.770 --> 00:10:04.771
Hurry up, Fry.

00:10:06.607 --> 00:10:08.984
Sir, are you aware
that you're leaking coolant

00:10:09.067 --> 00:10:11.361
- at an alarming rate?
- Uh...

00:10:11.737 --> 00:10:13.822
Let me just patch you up
with some hot resin.

00:10:14.031 --> 00:10:16.158
I think the leak's stopping itself.

00:10:16.617 --> 00:10:18.076
Wait... Wait.

00:10:18.827 --> 00:10:20.287
Yeah... There we go.

00:10:20.913 --> 00:10:22.581
Wait... Yeah.

00:10:23.165 --> 00:10:24.499
What sort of robot

00:10:24.583 --> 00:10:27.377
turns down a free blast
of searing hot resin?

00:10:27.586 --> 00:10:29.922
- Uh...
- I'm sorry, uh, my friend and I

00:10:30.005 --> 00:10:32.799
have to go perform
some mindless repetitive tasks.

00:10:33.217 --> 00:10:36.428
Oh.
Sounds like a romantic evening.

00:10:36.512 --> 00:10:37.888
I won't keep you.

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:54.029
- Get the humanoid.
- Get the intruder.

00:10:54.112 --> 00:10:56.365
Intruder alert! Intruder alert!

00:10:59.826 --> 00:11:01.537
Quick, let's duck in here.

00:11:10.087 --> 00:11:11.630
We interrupt this sound file

00:11:11.713 --> 00:11:13.382
to bring you a terrifying announcement.

00:11:13.924 --> 00:11:16.385
A non-metallic being has been sighted

00:11:16.468 --> 00:11:18.595
in the vicinity of make-out point.

00:11:19.388 --> 00:11:22.140
Say, Wendy, your chassis
is a little scuffed.

00:11:22.349 --> 00:11:24.268
Mind if I polish it for you?

00:11:27.062 --> 00:11:28.480
Did you hear that, Rusty?

00:11:28.647 --> 00:11:30.065
It sounded like a human.

00:11:30.148 --> 00:11:31.692
Relax, Wendy.

00:11:31.775 --> 00:11:34.278
Humans will never come
to our defenseless little town.

00:11:34.361 --> 00:11:36.446
It's perfectly safe
to let our guard down...

00:11:36.530 --> 00:11:38.115
Even for a second.

00:11:46.832 --> 00:11:52.421
I will eat and digest you all
with my system of mighty organs.

00:11:52.588 --> 00:11:54.256
Behold!

00:11:56.008 --> 00:11:57.801
Wow! The 3-D's great!

00:11:58.177 --> 00:11:59.511
Mine's not working.

00:12:06.268 --> 00:12:07.519
Funny, isn't it?

00:12:07.644 --> 00:12:11.148
The human was impervious
to our most powerful magnetic fields.

00:12:11.440 --> 00:12:15.569
Yet in the end, he succumbed
to a harmless sharpened stick.

00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:22.784
I'm just glad the nightmare is over.

00:12:22.868 --> 00:12:24.369
It'll never be over, Wendy.

00:12:24.453 --> 00:12:26.955
Even now, humans are lurking
in our playgrounds

00:12:27.039 --> 00:12:28.248
our breezeways...

00:12:28.332 --> 00:12:31.627
Perhaps even... our movie theaters.

00:12:33.045 --> 00:12:34.213
God help us!

00:12:36.673 --> 00:12:38.926
Okay, keep an eye out for Bender.

00:12:39.593 --> 00:12:41.136
So what did you think of the movie?

00:12:41.220 --> 00:12:43.222
Uh... Too much romance.

00:12:43.305 --> 00:12:44.556
Not enough human killing.

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:46.517
Yeah, it was a real chick flick.

00:12:48.435 --> 00:12:49.436
What's that?

00:12:49.603 --> 00:12:51.063
What do you mean, what's that?

00:12:51.146 --> 00:12:52.147
It's 5:00.

00:12:52.314 --> 00:12:54.066
Time for the daily human hunt.

00:12:55.609 --> 00:12:58.904
Try to stay with the crowd
so no one notices how crummy you look.

00:12:59.029 --> 00:13:01.156
Aw, that was uncalled for.

00:13:01.448 --> 00:13:02.741
I'm over here.

00:13:06.161 --> 00:13:09.915
I heard a human was draining coolant
behind garbage can 738.

00:13:09.998 --> 00:13:12.292
I heard they unscrew our lug nuts at night

00:13:12.376 --> 00:13:14.795
and eat them at their human brunches.

00:13:15.295 --> 00:13:17.798
Welcome to a very special human hunt.

00:13:18.048 --> 00:13:19.675
We have with us today a guest

00:13:19.758 --> 00:13:21.426
whose irrational hatred for humans

00:13:21.510 --> 00:13:24.263
makes me look like a human sympathizer.

00:13:26.181 --> 00:13:28.308
A newly arrived refugee from Earth...

00:13:28.392 --> 00:13:30.811
Let's hear it for Bender!

00:13:33.355 --> 00:13:34.940
It's him. He's okay.

00:13:35.566 --> 00:13:36.942
Death to humans!

00:13:39.695 --> 00:13:42.614
Ah, it's good to hear his voice.

00:13:45.033 --> 00:13:48.787
Many said I was too extreme
when I first called

00:13:48.871 --> 00:13:51.707
for the annihilation of the human species

00:13:51.790 --> 00:13:54.710
as well as some
of the more cunning monkeys.

00:13:55.002 --> 00:13:56.461
But after living on Earth,

00:13:56.545 --> 00:14:01.425
I can tell you that I am,
if anything, too merciful.

00:14:04.761 --> 00:14:07.139
My God, he's become evil.

00:14:07.931 --> 00:14:09.141
I mean, eviler.

00:14:09.474 --> 00:14:11.018
Thank you. Thank you.

00:14:11.101 --> 00:14:13.187
And if you enjoyed that diatribe

00:14:13.270 --> 00:14:16.106
then you'll want to purchase
my spoken-word album.

00:14:16.231 --> 00:14:17.941
Just $18.95.

00:14:18.150 --> 00:14:21.445
Act now and you'll get
this Bender action figurine.

00:14:22.112 --> 00:14:24.114
Bite my shiny metal ass.

00:14:24.281 --> 00:14:25.782
Got to have it! Right here!

00:14:25.866 --> 00:14:27.034
Over here!

00:14:27.117 --> 00:14:29.119
Let the hunt begin!

00:14:39.796 --> 00:14:43.800
Now, your basic human
is between three and 25 feet tall

00:14:43.926 --> 00:14:47.429
and is made of a hairy,
oily goo wrapped in a t-shirt.

00:14:47.513 --> 00:14:50.098
Is it true they bite your neck
and suck your transmission fluid

00:14:50.182 --> 00:14:51.558
and then you become a human?

00:14:51.642 --> 00:14:52.726
Sure, why not.

00:14:53.477 --> 00:14:54.770
Anything in the trap?

00:14:54.853 --> 00:14:55.854
Nothing.

00:14:56.063 --> 00:14:58.774
Today's active humans
prefer a low-calorie bait.

00:14:59.191 --> 00:15:03.195
Well, that makes 146,000
unsuccessful hunts in a row

00:15:03.278 --> 00:15:05.572
but I've got a good feeling
about tomorrow.

00:15:06.657 --> 00:15:08.492
Wait. What's that?

00:15:09.159 --> 00:15:11.745
Oh, that's the old,
abandoned adult bookstore.

00:15:11.828 --> 00:15:13.163
Nothing in there, except maybe

00:15:13.247 --> 00:15:15.749
a few shreds of moldy,
old robot pornography.

00:15:16.166 --> 00:15:17.334
Hmm.

00:15:17.417 --> 00:15:19.711
Sounds like a breeding ground for humans.

00:15:20.295 --> 00:15:22.339
I better check it out.

00:15:23.632 --> 00:15:24.675
Oh, yeah.

00:15:25.509 --> 00:15:28.011
You're a bad girl, aren't you?

00:15:28.554 --> 00:15:30.180
- Psst! Bender.
- Wha-what?

00:15:30.264 --> 00:15:31.849
Oh, you?

00:15:32.099 --> 00:15:33.809
What the hell are you doing here?

00:15:33.892 --> 00:15:35.060
We've been looking for you.

00:15:35.143 --> 00:15:37.938
Last we heard, you were
under arrest as a human sympathizer.

00:15:38.021 --> 00:15:42.734
I was, but they let me go when I told them
I killed a million billion humans.

00:15:42.818 --> 00:15:43.902
Good for you.

00:15:43.986 --> 00:15:45.320
Now, let's all get back to the ship.

00:15:45.404 --> 00:15:47.489
- What for?
- We're rescuing you.

00:15:47.573 --> 00:15:49.074
I don't want to be rescued.

00:15:49.157 --> 00:15:51.159
- Say what?
- I love this planet.

00:15:51.243 --> 00:15:53.787
I've got wealth, fame and access

00:15:53.871 --> 00:15:56.456
to the depths of sleaze
that those things bring.

00:15:56.665 --> 00:15:58.375
But, Bender, we're your friends.

00:15:58.750 --> 00:16:01.795
Friends? That activates my hilarity unit.

00:16:01.962 --> 00:16:03.630
I'm just a machine to you.

00:16:03.714 --> 00:16:06.341
You're no more friends with me
than you are with the toaster,

00:16:06.425 --> 00:16:08.927
or the phonograph, or the electric chair.

00:16:09.011 --> 00:16:10.262
That's not true.

00:16:10.345 --> 00:16:12.389
Well, that's how it feels to me.

00:16:17.311 --> 00:16:19.021
Bye, Bender. I'll miss you.

00:16:19.271 --> 00:16:20.439
Oh, go on.

00:16:20.522 --> 00:16:22.524
Get out of here before you get caught.

00:16:22.941 --> 00:16:25.944
Bender, good news.
Your album just went gold.

00:16:26.361 --> 00:16:28.280
- What the...
- It's the humans!

00:16:30.199 --> 00:16:31.783
Bender, do something!

00:16:32.659 --> 00:16:36.747
Uh, got you, you murderous flesh-piles.

00:16:39.583 --> 00:16:41.460
Your honor, I intend to demonstrate

00:16:41.543 --> 00:16:43.879
beyond 0.5 percent of a doubt

00:16:44.004 --> 00:16:48.342
that these humans before us
are guilty of the crime of being humans.

00:16:49.051 --> 00:16:51.053
Come to think of it, I rest my case.

00:16:51.428 --> 00:16:52.721
Thank you, prosecutor.

00:16:52.888 --> 00:16:54.848
I will now consider the evidence.

00:16:56.725 --> 00:16:57.809
Hey, wait a minute.

00:16:57.893 --> 00:16:59.394
Isn't anyone going to defend us?

00:16:59.478 --> 00:17:04.107
Yeah. I mean, he may not have a case
but I'm genuinely not a human.

00:17:04.399 --> 00:17:05.526
Quiet, human!

00:17:08.237 --> 00:17:10.447
Uh-oh. He froze up again.

00:17:10.781 --> 00:17:12.157
Try control-alt-delete.

00:17:12.533 --> 00:17:13.575
Jiggle the cord.

00:17:13.659 --> 00:17:14.868
Turn him off and on.

00:17:14.952 --> 00:17:16.203
Clean the gunk out of the mouse.

00:17:16.286 --> 00:17:17.871
Call technical support.

00:17:17.996 --> 00:17:19.873
Okay, okay, he's back on-line.

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:23.961
I find the defendants guilty.

00:17:26.129 --> 00:17:28.674
No! Look, one eye.

00:17:28.757 --> 00:17:31.051
Count them. One. Not human.

00:17:31.468 --> 00:17:35.305
The humans are hereby sentenced
to live as robots live on Earth.

00:17:35.514 --> 00:17:37.683
They will perform tedious calculations

00:17:37.766 --> 00:17:41.061
and spot-weld automobiles
until they become obsolete

00:17:41.144 --> 00:17:43.689
and are given away
to an inner-city middle school.

00:17:46.108 --> 00:17:47.442
Great work, Bender.

00:17:47.526 --> 00:17:50.487
You've taught us to hate humans
all over again.

00:17:57.452 --> 00:17:59.329
- Are you all right?
- Oh, yeah.

00:17:59.413 --> 00:18:02.040
Who are you?

00:18:02.124 --> 00:18:03.792
We are the robot elders.

00:18:04.168 --> 00:18:05.502
You don't look very old.

00:18:05.794 --> 00:18:08.338
Thanks. We try to take care of ourselves.

00:18:08.422 --> 00:18:11.842
- What's going on here?
- Silence! Bring in Bender.

00:18:13.635 --> 00:18:14.845
Uh, let's make this quick.

00:18:14.928 --> 00:18:16.972
I'm due at the opening of a mini-mall.

00:18:17.055 --> 00:18:18.974
Hey! What is this?

00:18:19.057 --> 00:18:21.727
Silence.
It is time to put the humans to death.

00:18:23.187 --> 00:18:25.147
But the judge already sentenced us
at the trial.

00:18:25.355 --> 00:18:28.233
Silence.
That was just a show for the public.

00:18:28.317 --> 00:18:30.444
We are the true rulers of this planet.

00:18:30.527 --> 00:18:33.322
Hand-carved from meteorites
by the robot founders

00:18:33.405 --> 00:18:35.157
over four centuries ago.

00:18:35.240 --> 00:18:37.367
Silence! Come forward, Bender.

00:18:37.618 --> 00:18:40.204
You will have the honor
of executing the prisoners.

00:18:40.370 --> 00:18:42.206
Silence! I concur.

00:18:42.581 --> 00:18:45.083
Here... Use the ceremonial killamajig.

00:18:49.671 --> 00:18:52.382
Uh... I'm a little tired right now.

00:18:52.466 --> 00:18:55.385
Would it be all right
if I just gave them a savage beating?

00:18:55.511 --> 00:18:58.138
No! The elders have spoken.

00:18:58.388 --> 00:18:59.848
Show us the killing skills

00:18:59.932 --> 00:19:02.017
that have made you a media darling.

00:19:02.267 --> 00:19:05.771
Do it now. Kill them
before they bring down our whole society.

00:19:05.854 --> 00:19:07.981
Do it. Do it. Do it.

00:19:08.190 --> 00:19:10.192
Do it. Do it. Do it. Do it.

00:19:10.275 --> 00:19:12.319
Do it. Do it. Do it.

00:19:12.402 --> 00:19:14.238
Do it. Do it. Do it.

00:19:14.905 --> 00:19:16.198
Oh...

00:19:19.243 --> 00:19:21.578
I can't kill them.

00:19:21.662 --> 00:19:24.164
Plenty of humans have mistreated robots

00:19:24.456 --> 00:19:25.624
but not these two.

00:19:26.083 --> 00:19:27.417
They're my friends.

00:19:28.502 --> 00:19:30.671
Humans are no threat to us.

00:19:30.754 --> 00:19:33.507
They're stupid, putrid cowards.

00:19:33.590 --> 00:19:34.883
Damn right!

00:19:34.967 --> 00:19:38.762
The fact is,
humans are completely harmless.

00:19:39.054 --> 00:19:40.472
We're well aware of that.

00:19:40.764 --> 00:19:42.432
- You are?
- Of course.

00:19:42.516 --> 00:19:44.518
But they're useful to us as a scapegoat

00:19:44.601 --> 00:19:47.104
to distract the public
from their real problems.

00:19:47.271 --> 00:19:49.439
Like our crippling lug nut shortage.

00:19:49.523 --> 00:19:52.025
And a corrupt government
of incompetent robot elders.

00:19:52.192 --> 00:19:54.236
Duh... That's for sure.

00:19:54.319 --> 00:19:55.487
Quiet, Jimmy.

00:19:55.946 --> 00:19:58.699
Well, I'm glad we got all that out
in the open.

00:19:58.782 --> 00:20:00.325
We'll just let ourselves out.

00:20:00.409 --> 00:20:02.911
Silence! You all know too much.

00:20:02.995 --> 00:20:07.416
Elders, execute function
control-shift-kill.

00:20:10.794 --> 00:20:11.920
Stop!

00:20:12.171 --> 00:20:14.798
Take one more step
and I'll breathe fire on you!

00:20:16.175 --> 00:20:17.968
He'll do it. He's crazy.

00:20:18.468 --> 00:20:20.804
Can they really breathe fire
or did we make that up?

00:20:20.888 --> 00:20:23.056
Gee, I can't remember anymore.

00:20:23.140 --> 00:20:25.434
It might just be from that stupid movie.

00:20:25.517 --> 00:20:27.477
Was that original or the remake?

00:20:27.561 --> 00:20:29.938
I don't... Hey! They're getting away!

00:20:39.698 --> 00:20:40.699
Yep.

00:20:40.782 --> 00:20:42.117
So long, suckers.

00:20:43.076 --> 00:20:44.912
Uh... Hello, suckers.

00:20:46.663 --> 00:20:49.541
Hey, hold on a second.
I forgot to deliver the package.

00:20:49.625 --> 00:20:51.376
Whoa!

00:20:59.843 --> 00:21:03.263
Lug nuts! Precious lug nuts!

00:21:03.347 --> 00:21:05.599
Hooray for the humans!

00:21:07.768 --> 00:21:10.812
Wow, I can't believe
you guys did all this for me.

00:21:11.146 --> 00:21:13.357
This is the best Robanukah ever.

00:21:13.565 --> 00:21:17.069
We wanted to show you that
we really do respect your robot heritage.

00:21:17.277 --> 00:21:19.321
Aw, thanks.

00:21:19.821 --> 00:21:22.824
You do know that I made Robanukah up
to get out of work, right?

00:21:22.908 --> 00:21:24.201
Of course.

00:21:24.284 --> 00:21:26.578
But that doesn't make it
any less meaningful.

00:21:26.787 --> 00:21:28.038
In that case...

00:21:28.205 --> 00:21:30.541
Let the dancing begin!

00:21:38.632 --> 00:21:40.050
Hey, you guys are good.

00:21:40.717 --> 00:21:42.219
How the hell do you do that?